  era: "Section 11 \xB7 Post-Gupta Period \xB7 c. 550 \u2013 1000 CE"
  title: Harshavardhana
  text: Harshavardhana ruled much of north India from Kannauj between 606 and 647 CE. Banabhatta wrote his biography, the Harshacharita, and the Chinese pilgrim Xuanzang described his court and the great assembly at Prayag. He was halted on the Narmada by Pulakeshin the Second.
